","partOfSpeechKo":"형용사","definitionKo":"주름이 많이 져 있다.","englishExpression":"crumpled; wrinkled","englishDescription":"Having a lot of creases.","sourceUrl":"https://krdict.korean.go.kr/eng/dicSearch/SearchView?ParaWordNo=40151&nation=eng&nationCode=6"},{"id":"krdict:41665:1","headword":"꼬깃꼬깃하다","partOfSpeech":"adjective","partOfSpeechKo":"형용사","definitionKo":"자잘한 금이 많이 생겨 있다.","englishExpression":"crumpled","englishDescription":"Having a lot of small creases.","sourceUrl":"https://krdict.korean.go.kr/eng/dicSearch/SearchView?ParaWordNo=41665&nation=eng&nationCode=6"}],"daughter-in-law":[{"id":"krdict:55540:1","headword":"며느리","partOfSpeech":"noun","partOfSpeechKo":"명사","definitionKo":"아들의 아내.","englishExpression":"daughter-in-law","englishDescription":"The wife of one's son.","sourceUrl":"https://krdict.korean.go.kr/eng/dicSearch/SearchView?ParaWordNo=55540&nation=eng&nationCode=6"},{"id":"krdict:71194:4","headword":"어미","partOfSpeech":"noun","partOfSpeechKo":"명사","definitionKo":"시부모가 아들에게 아내인 며느리를 이르는 말.","englishExpression":"daughter-in-law","englishDescription":"A word used by a parent to refer to his/her daughter-in-law when talking to his/her son.","sourceUrl":"https://krdict.korean.go.kr/eng/dicSearch/SearchView?ParaWordNo=71194&nation=eng&nationCode=6"},{"id":"krdict:71195:3","headword":"어멈","partOfSpeech":"noun","partOfSpeechKo":"명사","definitionKo":"(조금 대접하는 말로) 시부모가 자식이 있는 며느리를 이르거나 부르는 말.","englishExpression":"daughter-in-law","englishDescription":"(slightly respectful) A word used by parents to refer to or address their daughter-in law who has a child.","sourceUrl":"https://krdict.korean.go.kr/eng/dicSearch/SearchView?ParaWordNo=71195&nation=eng&nationCode=6"}],"dispel":[{"id":"krdict:61911:2","headword":"사르다","partOfSpeech":"verb","partOfSpeechKo":"동사","definitionKo":"어떤 것을 남김없이 없애 버리다.","englishExpression":"remove; take away; dispel","englishDescription":"To eliminate something completely.","sourceUrl":"https://krdict.korean.go.kr/eng/dicSearch/SearchVi